der":

- `qwen/qwen3.5-35b-a3b` (cloud) + `qwen3.5:35b` (local)
- `qwen/qwen3.5-122b-a10b` (cloud) + `qwen3.5:122b` (local)
- `qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b` (cloud, added 2026-04-30) + `qwen3.6:35b` (local)
- and others (Mistral Small 4, Gemma 4 31B, …)

Each pair has its own `architecture`, `context_window`, `params`, `license`,
`web_search` flags. These can drift out of sync when a model spec is updated
(e.g. registry corrected qwen3.5:9b architecture from `moe` to `dense`
2026-04-30 — only the local entry was wrong).

Decision deferred at the time so the 0134 Hy3 lineup could ship before the
2026-05-08 free-preview expiry. This ticket captures the refactor as a
follow-up.

## Proposed schema

```yaml
- id: "qwen3.6-35b-a3b"
  name: "Qwen 3.6 35B"
  provider: Alibaba
  country: CN
  architecture: moe
  params: "35B MoE (3B active)"
  size_class: medium
  license: open-apache
  context_window: 262144   # logical max; per-provider overrides allowed
  providers:
    - router: openrouter
      router_model: "qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b"
      price_per_mtok_in: 0.16
      price_per_mtok_out: 0.97
      web_search: true
    - router: ollama
      router_model: "qwen3.6:35b"
      price_per_mtok_in: 0.0
      price_per_mtok_out: 0.0
      quantization: Q4_K_M
```

Model-level fields stay flat. Provider-specific fields move under
`providers:`. Sweeps in `experiments.toml` reference the model `id` plus a
provider selector.

## Actions

1. Inventory all duplicate pairs in current `models.yaml` (~10 pairs).
2. Update the loader (`experiments/.../models.py` or wherever `models.yaml`
   is parsed) to accept the new schema; keep backward-compat for entries
   without a `providers:` block during the transition.
3. Update `experiments.toml` sweep entries to use `model_id` + `provider`
   instead of the current pinning by full slug. Test that existing sweeps
   still produce the same JobSpec.
4. Migrate `models.yaml` entries pair-by-pair, deleting the duplicate as
   each pair is consolidated. Per registry policy, comment-out (don't
   delete) — but the deletion target here is a redundancy, not a retired
   model, so a single migration commit is acceptable with a clear log.
5. Drop the backward-compat path once all entries migrated.

## Test

- `pytest experiments/tests/test_registry.py` — new schema parses, old
  schema parses, JobSpec built from both is identical.
- A dry-run sweep over a representative subset (3 pairs) produces the
  same model lookup results before vs. after migration.

## Exit criteria

- One entry per logical model in `models.yaml`.
- All sweeps in `experiments.toml` use `model_id` + `provider`.
- No duplicate-pair drift possible (loader rejects unknown top-level keys).
- Tests green.
